  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The idea is simple: have an audio output volume limiter built into VRChat to prevent malicious actors from destroying innocent people's ears with loud static/screaming.\nIf a certain decibel threshold is reached, the game should reduce its output volume down to acceptable levels so it gives players enough time to report the offending party or world. This also gives players enough time to enter safemode or adjust the volume on their own.\nThis audio limiter would impact the following audio sources:\n* Microphones\n* Avatars\n* Worlds\n* More?\nNow your question might be \"why is this a good idea if you can simply just enter safemode to mute sounds?\"\nA lot of people, especially newcomers, don't know how to quickly enter safemode. Entering safemode is also not done as easily when something loud is playing to attack your ears, as it can easily startle you and cause you to panic. Safemode also doesn't protect you from loud audio sources coming from worlds, e.g. media players.",
